---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
---
<Layout title="Enterprise data protection"><PageHero eyebrow="FOR THE ENTERPRISE" title="The business runs on files. Protect what’s inside them." text="Compromising storage alone does not produce a readable Cyber Reliant protected file. Access requires the correct fragments, protected cryptographic material and authorized reconstruction." number="02"><a class="button button-dark" href="/request-demo?interest=Enterprise">Discuss your environment <Arrow/></a></PageHero>
<section class="section container"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">ASSUME EXPOSURE. DESIGN FOR RESILIENCE.</span><h2>Three questions for<br/>your next threat model.</h2></div><p>Start with the exposure.<br/>Then examine the controls.</p></div><div class="editorial-rows"><article><span>01</span><h3>What if someone<br/>copies the stored data?</h3><div><p>Copying encrypted fragments does not supply the complete file-access process. Readable data requires the correct pieces, the required cryptographic material and authorized Cyber Reliant reconstruction.</p><span class="evaluation-note">Evaluate: storage access, fragment exposure and key boundaries.</span></div></article><article><span>02</span><h3>What if a malicious<br/>application asks to open it?</h3><div><p>Application policy controls entry to the Cyber Reliant access path. Its Windows filter participates in identifying fragments, obtaining required cryptographic material, decrypting and rebuilding the file.</p><span class="evaluation-note">Evaluate: application identity, policy enforcement and bypass paths.</span></div></article><article><span>03</span><h3>What if ransomware<br/>reaches the environment?</h3><div><p>The reconstruction path adds a barrier between reaching stored fragments and producing readable data. Application-level controls also govern which applications can enter that path.</p><span class="evaluation-note">Evaluate: read/write/delete behavior and recovery. File-access protection is not ransomware immunity or a backup replacement.</span></div></article></div></section>
<section class="dark-section"><div class="section container"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">EXPOSURE IS NOT THE SAME AS READABILITY</span><h2>Possessing the fragments<br/>is not possessing the file.</h2></div><p>Reconstruction requires the correct fragments, protected cryptographic material and the authorized Cyber Reliant path.</p></div><div class="threat-map" role="img" aria-label="Protected fragments may be exposed through compromised storage. Readable reconstruction follows a separate path involving cryptographic material and application policy. Unapproved application requests are blocked by policy; backup and recovery remain separate requirements."><div class="threat-source"><span class="tiny-label">COMPROMISED STORAGE</span><div class="cipher-matrix">{['A7','F2','9C','3E','B8','D1','6F','2A','E4'].map(t=><i>{t}</i>)}</div><strong>Protected fragments</strong><span class="threat-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></div><div class="threat-paths"><div class="threat-path"><span class="risk-marker">EXFILTRATION SCENARIO</span><h3>Stored fragments are copied.</h3><p>The copied pieces remain encrypted fragments. Storage access alone does not supply the cryptographic material and authorized process required to rebuild the file.</p></div><div class="threat-path"><span class="risk-marker">MALICIOUS APPLICATION SCENARIO</span><h3>An unapproved app requests access.</h3><p>Application policy governs entry to reconstruction. Reaching protected storage does not automatically reproduce the Cyber Reliant file-access process.</p></div></div><div class="threat-boundary"><span>CONTROLLED RECONSTRUCTION</span><strong>Correct fragments + protected cryptographic material + authorized Cyber Reliant path</strong><p>A complete reconstruction process—not an ordinary storage read.</p></div></div><p class="threat-recovery"><span>RECOVERY IS A SEPARATE REQUIREMENT</span> File-access protection does not guarantee protection from deletion, storage outages or ransomware disruption. Retain and test backup and recovery controls.</p></div></section><section class="soft-section"><div class="section container"><span class="eyebrow">PRIORITIZE WHAT MATTERS</span><h2>Different files.<br/>Material consequences.</h2><div class="use-case-grid"><article><span class="use-case-symbol"><svg class="diagonal-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></span><h3>Intellectual property</h3><p>Engineering designs, research records and strategic plans whose exposure can erode a competitive advantage.</p></article><article><span class="use-case-symbol">≋</span><h3>Regulated information</h3><p>Financial, personal and health-related files that require carefully scoped access and a documented security evaluation.</p></article><article><span class="use-case-symbol">⌘</span><h3>Business operations</h3><p>Contracts, transaction records and internal working files shared across essential applications and teams.</p></article></div><p class="small-note">Use cases describe evaluation priorities, not compliance certifications or validated integrations.</p></div></section>
<section class="section container split-content"><div><span class="eyebrow">DESIGNED FOR A SERIOUS EVALUATION</span><h2>Bring the hard<br/>questions.</h2><p>A useful demonstration begins with your workflows, not a generic feature tour.</p><a class="text-link" href="/request-demo?interest=Enterprise">Plan a technical conversation <Arrow/></a></div><ol class="numbered-list"><li><strong>Map your sensitive file workflows</strong><p>Identify applications, users, storage locations and the boundaries that matter.</p></li><li><strong>Examine the protection and access path</strong><p>Trace the file path, the key path and the Windows filter’s role in reconstructing readable data.</p></li><li><strong>Define measurable acceptance criteria</strong><p>Test compatibility, performance, failure behavior and recovery in your intended deployment.</p></li></ol></section><CTA title="Build the evaluation around your business."/></Layout>
